# Project Overview  <a name="overview-main"></a>

### Context <a name="overview-context"></a>

As an avid Chelsea fan, I wanted to create some visualisations to better understand the way that they play football. Using publicly available Wyscout data, I researched their immensely disappointing 2015/2016 season. One to forget for Chelsea, but a season immortalised by Leicester's 5000/1 rise to the Premier League title.

Chelsea were not to wait too long for their next success however, with Antonio Conte implementing an imperious three-at-the-back system in the following season, leading to another title win. Incidentally, it is the last we have won since.

This project uses Python to sort through the data, extract their key passes, and plot heat maps, pass maps and a handy bar chart to garner Chelsea's most effective playmakers throughout the season.
